# cabin_quinault: home, the old ranger cabin at Lake Quinault, in August
# (BUILD_PLAN S7; GAME_DESIGN 2.2, 11.11; decision 70: a hand-drawn hero).
# A tall plate, 160x320 (doc 11.2). Drawn from 11.11's written brief and
# the spec's words for the architecture (a steep, nearly A-frame cedar
# gable; board and batten; the arched window high in the gable; two banks
# of three tall windows either side of a screen door; a raised deck with
# four pale chairs; the small matching shed to the right; the green tub at
# the porch's right corner; the iron fire bowl on a meadow of mole hills;
# huge mossy bigleaf maples, a towering Sitka spruce behind the roof and a
# snow-dusted rocky peak above the trees). Nothing is traced or sampled
# from any photo; no sign, number, road or shoreline places it.
#
# The plate draws no sky: web/js/gfx/cabin.js puts the hour's sky stamp on
# the sky layer, then the stars and the moon, and composes the lights, the
# smoke, the embers, the states and the weather over these layers, at the
# at_<name> anchors below. Light comes from the upper left, so faces turned
# left are lit. Each farther band is a step lighter; outlines are drawn in
# each shape's own color, then filled; nearer shapes on a layer come first
# where a farther fill has to flood around them.
#
# Rows 0 to 28 are quiet sky for the name over the cabin (lead call 61).

@ far
# The foothills: a hazy teal band across the valley with a ragged forested
# top, high enough that the roof's rakes stand against teal (slate at
# night), so the ink roof and the spruce read against it (spec 5.6, 9).
